  "root_cause_conclusion": "A-2 RL policy motion vector variance collapsed (other_motion std_y=0.0154 vs A-1 reference 0.678 and exp3 Cycler A-2 reference 0.690 -- a ~44x reduction), not a position-coverage problem (position correlation between A-1/A-2 measured near-zero, ruling out that hypothesis). MG has almost no learnable signal in the y-axis, produces inaccurate om fed directly into SM process-2 (original-paper wiring), which corrupts h2. Vision reconstruction losses are simultaneously BETTER than exp3 (self_vision 11.65 vs 16.79), consistent with h2 falling back on directly-visible A-1 features rather than a genuine other-state representation. MG error-by-position is roughly uniformly moderate across A-2 actual operating region (no sharp localized failure), consistent with a general signal-diversity problem rather than a regional one."
